# Git and deployment authority

- One writer per branch. Future product work uses `feat|fix|refactor|docs|ops/<DE000>_<scope>`.
- `main` is canonical integrated code. Agents must not push `main` during normal development.
- Do not commit, push, merge, rebase, force-push, rewrite history, drop stashes, or delete branches unless the current task explicitly authorizes that action.
- Merges to `main` require human review. Do not bypass branch protection.
- Git authority is not deployment authority. Do not deploy or mutate production config unless authorized.
- Preserve unrelated work. Inspect the diff and scan for secrets before any approved Git write.
- Tracked: sanitized `.ai/*.md` and `.cursor/rules/`. Ignored: `.ai/private/`, `.ai/local/`, `HANDOFF.md`, `CHANGELOG_SESSION.md`, `.env*`.
